--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold] + [temp.variadic]/5: a fold expression over a
function parameter pack in a MEMBER function template's body is now
reduced, when the member is instantiated, into the correctly-associated
binary expression over the pack's elements (right/left association per
[expr.prim.fold]/1-2, binary folds left-associated per /2, operator
identity for the empty pack per /3).  Previously the member-body
pack-expander (prepare_deferred_method_body) -- unlike the free-function
one in cpp_instantiate_template -- had no fold handling, so the fold's
bare pack reference failed to resolve and the body was dropped ("no body
for callee").  Covers arities 0/1/N and right/left/binary folds; all
values g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  The enclosing class need not be a
template.
